# D-FREED-INODE-HOME-NEVER-PUBLISHED-LIVE-CORE-AFTER-CLEAN-UNMOUNT: the CAW
# half of the final verification, 2/disk/caw/direct and 2/disk/caw/mpath on
# g2b, on the build of the final source: srcversion F09C3FED2DB371E0D9A8BC5
# (main tree ~/src/mxfs, 0.90.131: the H-F11 fix, both halves of the fix for
# D-RECYCLE-RESET-UNDER-NOINO-STRANDS-COMMITTED-DIR-CHANGE-WEDGE-SHUTDOWN, the
# unlinked-list fixes of
# D-PEER-OPEN-UNLINKED-CHAIN-REMOVE-FAILS-IFREE-SHUTDOWN-BOTH-NODES, and the
# deferred-free fixes of
# D-INACT-DEFERRED-FREE-LOSES-TRUNCATED-CORE-AND-REAP-AUTHORITY, all at their
# defaults; run from ~/src/mxfs, the harness prints each lap's build and
# refuses a node running anything else).  The record reaches every
# configuration; every corrupt lap so far was on TCP.  These laps run the TCP
# half's production settings on both CAW attachments: every guard at its
# module default 1 (noino_gen0_guard, inact_local_epoch_guard,
# noino_recycle_guard, freshsrc_keep_guard, selfclobber_keep_guard,
# noino_resv_guard, noino_shell_guard, pub_claim_release_guard,
# pub_claim_write_guard, deadshell_sanitize_guard, p55c_home_restore,
# noino_recycle_dirty_wait, noino_recycle_takeover, freshsrc_iunl_overlay,
# unlprev_tenure, b6_release_drain, unlprev_pin, unlprev_rele_defer,
# ifree_defer_drain, ifree_defer_reap), no window held open,
# mirror check on so the H-F7/H-F10 counters read.  NG0_P55C_RESTORE and
# NG0_DIRTY_WAIT are not set (the knobs stay at their default 1; see the TCP
# half's queue for why); the harness keeps H-F11's lines and chain and the
# dirty-corpse lines on every lap.  Node failures are counted from each node's
# whole kernel log after the lap's mark in both harnesses.
#
# The previous run of this half (build 737E182A809291DAA0B4785, labels
# fxcd1..fxcm3): every noino lap VACUOUS by its generation-0 gate, both
# peer-last-closer laps PASS; it ran before the recycle fix, so it does not
# speak for this build.  The run on build C06A6D4A9AB7A357503DF51 (labels
# fycd1..fycm3) was 8 of 8 cold audits CLEAN with hf11_chain 0; it ran before
# the unlinked-list fixes, which change the inactivation and unlinked-list
# paths every lap here exercises, so it does not speak for this build either.
# The run on build 41D2F9237EBB21CF21E9D57 (labels fzcd1..fzcm3, log
# tests/evidence/lapq_fzc.log) audited CORRUPT in every noino lap (logged
# VACUOUS by the generation-0 gate, which then printed no audit; harness since
# fixed), with every audited inode a free deferred at the unlinked-list
# preflight: D-INACT-DEFERRED-FREE-LOSES-TRUNCATED-CORE-AND-REAP-AUTHORITY,
# whose two fixes this build carries.  Both peer-last-closer laps passed.
#
# THE DEFERRED-FREE GRADING (added for build 311877C4, before its first lap).
# A free deferred at the unlinked-list preflight leaves its inode on its AGI
# bucket, and tools/chk_mxfs grades a bucket member as legal crash residue, not
# an error, so a CLEAN audit alone cannot show that the deferred inodes were
# freed.  Every noino lap therefore also sets NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1
# NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 (the module defaults, written and read back): the harness
# then attributes every bucket member and fork-ownership error to the
# deferrals that name it (tools/ifree_defer_attribution.py) and passes the lap
# only with no fork-ownership error, no unlanded drain and no bucket member
# left (if_ok=1).  The deferrals' reach (20 to 30 a lap on CAW on the previous
# build) is then those laps' vacuity gate, in place of the generation-0
# release's, which CAW never reached.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   CLEAN     every lap's cold audit CLEAN errors=0 with node_failures=0 and
#             hf11_chain=0, and every noino lap if_ok=1 with if_zombies=0 and
#             if_fork_errors=0.  A noino lap graded VACUOUS by the deferrals'
#             reach gate keeps its cold audit and hf11_chain as its verdict and
#             is reported as unreached.  The peer-last-closer
#             laps must pass their harness (PASS, ZRESULT not ZFAIL) and reach
#             the H-F6 branch (inact_peerfreed > 0 in aggregate).
#   REACH     p55_restored_lof per lap (H-F11 on CAW: the H-F11 A/B's CAW
#             control xcc1 did not reach it), the guards' counters, and the
#             dirty-corpse lines (P-RECYCLE-DIRTY-WAIT/KEEP/TAKEOVER,
#             P-NOINO-TAKEN-OVER).
#   CORRUPT   any CORRUPT audit, hf11_chain > 0, or P-RECYCLE-RESET-UNDER-NOINO
#             with owes=1 blocks the record: attribute the audited inode
#             (chk_audit.log, <node>_audited_inos.txt) or the line to a known
#             shape or a new one.
#   UNSTABLE  any node failure line in a lap's whole kernel log: blocks both
#             records until attributed.
# A lap whose audit is STALE/NONE has no verdict and is rerun.
#
# The run on build 311877C431E1BB444562804 (labels fwcd1..fwcm3, log
# tests/evidence/lapq_fwc.log) was 7 of 8 PASS: lap fwcm3 (2/disk/caw/mpath)
# FAILED if_ok=0 with six deferred zombies left on AG 1 bucket 1 after the clean
# unmount, each one's reap entry retired by a lookup that met its in-core inode
# queued for inactivation: H-3 of
# D-INACT-DEFERRED-FREE-LOSES-TRUNCATED-CORE-AND-REAP-AUTHORITY, whose change
# (reap_transient_keep, default 1) this build carries along with H-U7 of
# D-PEER-OPEN-UNLINKED-CHAIN-REMOVE-FAILS-IFREE-SHUTDOWN-BOTH-NODES
# (reload_next_refresh, default 1) and a publish-drain instrument (no behaviour
# change).  This run (labels fucm1..fucd3) puts the mpath laps first: the
# direct laps of tests/queues/peer_open_unlinked_final_g_caw.queue hold
# run.sh's 2/disk/caw/direct lock on g2d while it starts.  The rules below are
# unchanged; under H-3's change a lap also fails on any reap entry retired by a
# transient lookup failure (if_retired_transient > 0, the harness's if_ok).
#
# The run on build F09C3FED2DB371E0D9A8BC5 (labels fucm1..fucd3, log
# tests/evidence/lapq_fuc.log) was 8 of 8 PASS.  This run (labels fvc*,
# written before its first lap) is on build 37897D38118AD5E2FAAC4FC (main tree
# ~/src/mxfs, 0.90.131): that source plus every change made since, each at its
# module default.  Behaviour: H-F13's inode-allocation fence with its revision
# H-F13b (ag_ialloc_fence 1, ag_fence_hint_exempt 1), H-F12's bounded drain
# built but off (pub_drain_bound 0, the open scan every earlier run had), and
# the fixes of D-CREATE-REUSE-OVER-PEER-FREED-LINKED-CORPSE-SHUTS-NODE-DOWN
# (cr63_linked_defer), D-UMOUNT-ROOT-DENTRY-STILL-IN-USE-DEFERRED-DIR-DCACHE-SHRINK-RACE
# (dshrink_umount_gate), D-NETMESH-LIVE-FILE-INODE-FREED-UNDER-ITS-NAME-AFTER-NUMBER-REUSE
# (sf_kept_ahead_base) and D-FORMATION-RAMP-LOCK-REQUEST-EXHAUSTS-RETRIES-EAGAIN
# (ilock_retry_exhaust_park, dl_retry_view_unspent).  Instruments only: the
# handoff exposure census (P-PUB-UNPUB-AT-UNLOCK), the phantom detector's
# in-flight sample and the next-write detector's own-free exception.  The
# direct laps go first this time: the dentry-race A/B
# (tests/queues/umount_dshrink_race_ab.queue) holds run.sh's 2/disk/caw/mpath
# lock on g2d while this queue starts.  The rules above are unchanged.
#
# Bounds: noino laps 1680 s (the TCP half's derivation: 1660 + the P55C stream
# pass 2x10); the peer-last-closer laps 1130 s (the H-F6 queue's 1090 + 2x20
# for the sanitize knob set/readback).
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh fvcd1 1 300 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=1 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh fvcl2 1 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh fvcd2 1 300 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh fvcm1 1 300 2/disk/caw/mpath g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=1 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh fvcl1 1 40 2/disk/caw/mpath g2b
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh fvcm2 1 300 2/disk/caw/mpath g2b
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh fvcd3 1 300 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh fvcm3 1 300 2/disk/caw/mpath g2b
